hadiths[5]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16588","He said: Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us, he said: Aban, he is al-Attar, narrated to us, he said: Yahya, meaning Ibn Abi Kathir, narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Zayd, that his father narrated to him that he witnessed the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, at the slaughter place, and a man of Quraysh, while he was distributing sacrifices, but nothing of them befell him nor his companion, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, shaved his head in his garment and gave it to him, so he distributed of it upon men, and clipped his nails and gave them to his companion, he said: For indeed it is with us dyed with henna and katam, meaning his hair."
"16589","He said: Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, he said: Aban al-Attar narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, that Abu Salamah narrated to him that Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Zayd informed him, from his father, that he witnessed the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, at the slaughter place, he and a man of the Ansar, so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, distributed sacrifices, but nothing befell him nor his companion, so he shaved his head in his garment and gave it to him, and distributed of it upon men, and clipped his nails and gave them to his companion, for indeed his hair is with us dyed with henna and katam."
"16590","He said: Zayd ibn al-Hubab Abu al-Husayn al-Ukli narrated to us, he said: Abu Sahl Muhammad ibn Amr informed me, he said: Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Zayd informed me, from his uncle Abdullah ibn Zayd, that he was shown the adhan, he said: So I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and informed him, so he said: Cast it upon Bilal, so I cast it, and he called the adhan, he said: Then he wanted to establish, so I said: O Messenger of Allah, I saw it, I want to establish, he said: Then establish yourself, so he established and Bilal called the adhan."
"16591","He said: Yaqub narrated to us, he said: My father informed us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: And Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Zuhri mentioned, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Abdullah ibn Zayd ibn Abd Rabbihi, he said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, resolved to strike with the bell to gather the people for prayer, while he disliked it for its agreement with the Christians, one visiting at night visited me while I was sleeping, a man upon him two green garments, and in his hand a bell carrying it, he said: So I said to him: O servant of Allah, do you sell the bell, he said: And what do you do with it, I said: We call with it to prayer, he said: Shall I not guide you to better than that, he said: So I said: Yes indeed, he said: You say: Allah is Most Great, Allah is Most Great, Allah is Most Great, Allah is Most Great, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, come to prayer, come to prayer, come to success, come to success, Allah is Most Great, Allah is Most Great, there is no god but Allah, he said: Then I withdrew not far, he said: Then you say when you establish the prayer: Allah is Most Great, Allah is Most Great, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, come to prayer, come to success, the prayer has been established, the prayer has been established, Allah is Most Great, Allah is Most Great, there is no god but Allah, he said: So when morning came, I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and informed him of what I saw, he said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Indeed this is a true vision, if Allah wills, then he ordered the call to prayer, so Bilal, the freed slave of Abu Bakr, used to call the adhan with that and call the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, to prayer, he said: So he came to him and called him one morning to Fajr, so it was said to him: Indeed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, is sleeping, he said: So Bilal cried with his highest voice: Prayer is better than sleep, Said ibn al-Musayyab said: So this phrase was entered in the call to prayer for the Fajr prayer."
"16592","He said: Yaqub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, he said: Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith al-Taymi narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Zayd ibn Abd Rabbihi, he said: Abdullah ibn Zayd narrated to me, he said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered the bell to be struck with it for the people in gathering for prayer, one visited me while I was sleeping, a man carrying a bell in his hand, so I said to him: O servant of Allah, do you sell the bell, he said: What do you do with it, he said: So I said: We call with it to prayer, he said: Shall I not guide you to what is better than that, he said: So I said to him: Yes indeed, he said: You say: Allah is Most Great, Allah is Most Great, Allah is Most Great, Allah is Most Great, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, come to prayer, come to prayer, come to success, come to success, Allah is Most Great, Allah is Most Great, there is no god but Allah, then he withdrew not far, then he said: You say when the prayer is established: Allah is Most Great, Allah is Most Great, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, come to prayer, come to success, the prayer has been established, the prayer has been established, Allah is Most Great, Allah is Most Great, there is no god but Allah, so when morning came, I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and informed him of what I saw, so he said: Indeed it is a true vision, if Allah wills, so stand with Bilal and cast upon him what you saw, let him call the adhan with it, for indeed he is more melodious in voice than you, he said: So I stood with Bilal and kept casting it upon him and he called the adhan with it, he said: So Umar ibn al-Khattab heard of that while he was in his house, so he went out dragging his cloak, saying: By the One who sent you with the truth, I have seen like what he was shown, he said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Then praise be to Allah."
